From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aiueo52 <aiueo52@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 17:23:14 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 063/105] adaptive: post-switch grace window + retuned
 two-state config

Measured on Qwen3.8-Flash-Next: a swap leaves the draft cold (its per-step
KV branches and the state's QSA shared-index buffer were built for the other
step count), so the verifies right after it under-report acceptance. With a
5-batch decision interval the controller was reading its own transient and
flipping back every interval.

- AdaptiveStepSlot.switch_grace_batches: hold decisions for N batches after
  a switch. The EMA keeps updating through the window; only the decision is
  deferred, so the next one sees the new setting's steady state.
- adaptive_w16_3_15.json: ema_alpha 0.1, update_interval 20,
  switch_grace_batches 40, no EMA reseed (the carried EMA is what lets the
  window measure rather than probe).
- dbg/sim.py: offline controller simulation against the measured
  per-workload accept distributions and the 9.74 + 0.70*S ms/iteration cost
  model; reproduces the fixed-profile throughputs within 5%.
- SGLANG_ADAPTIVE_DEBUG=1 logs what the EMA actually saw per decision
  (samples seen/kept, mean, histogram) -- how the ping-pong was diagnosed.
- Two upstream unit tests fed accept counts above the live step count, which
  the stale-sample filter now drops; retargeted them at reachable values.

